From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Put the W541's USB connectors on their
 sides

The _PLD of the four USB connectors come from the OEM tables, which the
T440p and the W541 share. Moving a USB 3.0 drive through the W541's
connectors with PORTSC watched puts three of them on another panel than
those buffers say: port 1 (HS01/SS01, the one the OEM tables mark as
the Always On port) is the second connector on the left side counted
from the screen, not on the right; port 2 (HS02/SS02) is the lower
connector on the right side, not on the left; port 3 (HS03) is the
first connector on the left side, not on the back; port 6 (HS06) is the
upper connector on the right, as said. The OS shows the position to
the user only (Windows's port names, Linux's physical_location), so
nothing else changes.

Give the W541 buffers with the measured panels: left for ports 1 and 3,
with the horizontal position telling the two apart as seen facing that
side, right for ports 2 and 6, lower and upper. The shape is a USB-A
connector's, the group positions and the rest of the bytes stay the
OEM's. The T440p keeps the OEM buffers until someone measures it.

TEST=iasl -tc -w3: the buffers compile and disassemble to LEFT/CENTER/
RIGHT, RIGHT/LOWER/CENTER, LEFT/CENTER/LEFT and RIGHT/UPPER/CENTER on
the W541, the OEM values on the T440p.
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl | 46 +++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl
index 1531df4b..85ae7a3e 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/usb.asl
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
  * 2 left, 3 right, 4 front, 5 back) and VerticalPosition (6-7); byte 9 has
  * HorizontalPosition (bits 0-1) and Shape (2-5).
  *
- *  xHCI port  USB 3.0  OEM     connector
+ *  xHCI port  USB 3.0  OEM     connector, as the OEM tables say
  *  1          16       UPC0    USB 3.0, right (the Always On one)
  *  2          17       UPC1    USB 3.0, left
  *  3          -        UPC2    USB 2.0, back
@@ -25,6 +25,14 @@
  *  12         -        -       inside: the camera
  *  4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 14, 15, USB 3.0 18, 19, 21: nothing
  *
+ * On the W541 the four connectors are not where those buffers put them,
+ * measured by moving a drive through them with PORTSC watched: port 1 is
+ * the second connector on the left side, counted from the screen (the OEM
+ * tables mark it as the Always On one); port 2 is the lower connector on
+ * the right side; port 3 is the first connector on the left side; port 6
+ * the upper one on the right. The W541 gets buffers with those panels and
+ * positions, the T440p keeps the OEM ones until someone measures it.
+ *
  * The OEM firmware marks the ports of the devices inside as not
  * connectable (what _UPC means by "nothing can ever be plugged there");
  * here they are connectable, with the OEM connector type, and not visible:
@@ -56,12 +64,36 @@
 #define PLD_EXPRESSCARD	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x48, 0x1D, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0, 0, 0
 #define PLD_INSIDE	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x30, 0x1C, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0, 0, 0
 
-USB_PORT(HS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_RIGHT)
-USB_PORT(HS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_LEFT)
-USB_PORT(HS03, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_USB2_BACK)
+#if CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541)
+/*
+ * The W541's connectors where they are. Byte 8: visible, the panel and the
+ * vertical position; byte 9: the horizontal position, as seen facing that
+ * side (on the left side "left" is towards the screen), and the shape of a
+ * USB-A connector (4, a horizontal rectangle); bytes 10-11 the OEM group
+ * positions of the two USB 3.0 ports; byte 12 as in the OEM buffers.
+ */
+/* Port 1: left side, the second connector from the screen */
+#define PLD_PORT1	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x51, 0x12, 0x80, 0x00, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+/* Port 2: right side, the lower connector */
+#define PLD_PORT2	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x99, 0x11, 0x00, 0x01, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+/* Port 3: left side, the first connector from the screen */
+#define PLD_PORT3	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x51, 0x10, 0x00, 0x00, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+/* Port 6: right side, the upper connector */
+#define PLD_PORT6	0x81, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x19, 0x11, 0x00, 0x00, 0x03, 0, 0, 0
+#else
+/* The T440p: the OEM buffers, until someone measures its connectors */
+#define PLD_PORT1	PLD_USB3_RIGHT
+#define PLD_PORT2	PLD_USB3_LEFT
+#define PLD_PORT3	PLD_USB2_BACK
+#define PLD_PORT6	PLD_USB2_RIGHT
+#endif
+
+USB_PORT(HS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT1)
+USB_PORT(HS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT2)
+USB_PORT(HS03, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_PORT3)
 USB_PORT(HS04, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS05, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
-USB_PORT(HS06, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_USB2_RIGHT)
+USB_PORT(HS06, USB_YES, USB_2_A, PLD_PORT6)
 USB_PORT(HS07, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS08, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS09, USB_YES, USB_OEM, PLD_DOCK)
@@ -71,8 +103,8 @@ USB_PORT(HS12, USB_YES, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS13, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS14, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(HS15, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
-USB_PORT(SS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_RIGHT)
-USB_PORT(SS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_USB3_LEFT)
+USB_PORT(SS01, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT1)
+USB_PORT(SS02, USB_YES, USB_3_A, PLD_PORT2)
 USB_PORT(SS03, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(SS04, USB_NO, USB_OEM, PLD_INSIDE)
 USB_PORT(SS05, USB_YES, USB_OEM, PLD_DOCK)
-- 
2.43.0

